<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof for Theorem 4.1 and Insights for Conjecture 4.1</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Bayes optimal 0-1 loss in terms of Overlapping Coefficient</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Bayes optimal classifier minimizes the 0-1 loss, predicting the class with the higher posterior probability at each <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. So the Bayes classifier <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> predicts:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}(x)=\arg\max_{y\in\{0,1\}}P_{y}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}(x)=\arg\max_{y\in\{0,1\}}P_{y}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the Bayes 0-1 loss <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as the expected probability of misclassification:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[\min(P_{0}(x),P_{1}(x))\right]=\sum_{x}\min(\pi_{0}P_{0}(x),\pi_{1}P_{1}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[\min(P_{0}(x),P_{1}(x))\right]=\sum_{x}\min(\pi_{0}P_{0}(x),\pi_{1}P_{1}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are class priors for both classes. Assuming identical class priors, we can simplify it as,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}=\dfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x}\min(P_{0}(x),P_{1}(x))=\dfrac{1}{2}OVL(P_{0},P_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}=\dfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x}\min(P_{0}(x),P_{1}(x))=\dfrac{1}{2}OVL(P_{0},P_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, for the two neighbouring datasets:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{1}=\dfrac{1}{2}OVL^{1}_{\text{train}},\quad L^{*}_{2}=\dfrac{1}{2}OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{1}=\dfrac{1}{2}OVL^{1}_{\text{train}},\quad L^{*}_{2}=\dfrac{1}{2}OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, if <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{1}\geq L^{*}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{1}\geq L^{*}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OVL^{1}_{\text{train}}\geq OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OVL^{1}_{\text{train}}\geq OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Overlapping coefficient is higher for <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{1}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{1}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We know from our second assumption that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta^{*}_{1},(x^{1}_{0},y^{1}_{0}))\geq L(\theta^{*}_{2},(x^{2}_{0},y^{2}_{0}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta^{*}_{1},(x^{1}_{0},y^{1}_{0}))\geq L(\theta^{*}_{2},(x^{2}_{0},y^{2}_{0})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since all other training examples are shared between the two datasets, the only difference in their total empirical losses lies in this one datapoint. Thus, the empirical loss satisfies:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{1}\geq L^{*}_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{1}\geq L^{*}_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From the derivation in Step 1, we thus get:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OVL^{1}_{\text{train}}\geq OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OVL^{1}_{\text{train}}\geq OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Subset relationship from loss dominance</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{1}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{1}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> differ in only one datapoint, we can write:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(L(\theta,(x^{1}_{0},y^{1}_{0}))+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}L(\theta,(x_{j},y_{j}))\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(L(\theta,(x^{1}_{0},y^{1}_{0}))+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}L(\theta,(x_{j},y_{j}))\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{D^{2}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{D^{2}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(L(\theta,(x^{2}_{0},y^{2}_{0}))+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}L(\theta,(x_{j},y_{j}))\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(L(\theta,(x^{2}_{0},y^{2}_{0}))+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}L(\theta,(x_{j},y_{j}))\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Subtracting:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)-L_{D^{2}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{n}\left(L(\theta,(x^{1}_{0},y^{1}_{0}))-L(\theta,(x^{2}_{0},y^{2}_{0}))\right)\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)-L_{D^{2}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{n}\left(L(\theta,(x^{1}_{0},y^{1}_{0}))-L(\theta,(x^{2}_{0},y^{2}_{0}))\right)\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">by the assumed loss inequality in our first assumption. Therefore:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{D^{2}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)\leq L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)\leq\epsilon\quad\Rightarrow\quad\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{D^{2}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)\leq L_{D^{1}_{\text{train}}}(\theta)\leq\epsilon\quad\Rightarrow\quad\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since this holds for all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math>, but not necessarily the other way around, we conclude:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Extension to <math id="A1.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-neighbouring datasets</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{1}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{1}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-neighbouring binary classification datasets, i.e., they differ at <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> indices <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for all <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j})\neq(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j})\neq(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and for all other <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\notin\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\notin\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, the examples are shared:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j})=(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j})=(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose further that the per-point loss dominance condition holds at all differing indices:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta,(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j}))\geq L(\theta,(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j}))\quad\forall\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\cup\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)},\quad\forall j\in\mathcal{I}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta,(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j}))\geq L(\theta,(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j}))\quad\forall\theta\in\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\cup\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)},\quad\forall j\in\mathcal{I}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta^{*}_{1},(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j}))\geq L(\theta^{*}_{2},(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j}))\quad\forall j\in\mathcal{I}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta^{*}_{1},(x^{1}_{j},y^{1}_{j}))\geq L(\theta^{*}_{2},(x^{2}_{j},y^{2}_{j}))\quad\forall j\in\mathcal{I}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then the overlapping coefficient between the classes is higher for <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{1}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{1}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OVL^{1}_{\text{train}}\geq OVL^{2}_{\text{train}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OVL^{1}_{\text{train}}\geq OVL^{2}_{\text{train}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and the Rashomon set satisfies:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To prove this, we can simply decompose the <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-neighbouring datasets into a sequence of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-neighbouring transitions:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{1}_{\text{train}}=D^{(0)}\to D^{(1)}\to\dots\to D^{(k)}=D^{2}_{\text{train}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{1}_{\text{train}}=D^{(0)}\to D^{(1)}\to\dots\to D^{(k)}=D^{2}_{\text{train}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> differ at exactly one datapoint <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t},y_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t},y_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss dominance condition holds at each step. From Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Theoretical Insights for Binary Classification ‣ 4 Higher Overlap leads to a Smaller Rashomon Set ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, each such one-step transition satisfies:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{(D^{(t)},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{(t+1)},\epsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{(D^{(t)},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{(t+1)},\epsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Applying this sequentially:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}=\Theta_{(D^{(0)},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{(1)},\epsilon)}\subseteq\dots\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{(k)},\epsilon)}=\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}=\Theta_{(D^{(0)},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{(1)},\epsilon)}\subseteq\dots\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{(k)},\epsilon)}=\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mtext>train</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{(D^{1}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}\subseteq\Theta_{(D^{2}_{\text{train}},\epsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Pseudocode for Algorithms</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>MultLow and MultHigh for Data Acquisition</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> MultLow for Data Acquisition</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Labeled dataset <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, unlabeled dataset <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, query size <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, committee size <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             Train a committee of <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> models <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{1},M_{2},\dots,M_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{1},M_{2},\dots,M_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in U</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Compute confidence <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> from each model <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Compute maximum confidence across all models: <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\max}(x)=\max_{i}c_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\max}(x)=\max_{i}c_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             Select bottom-<math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> points with lowest <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\max}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\max}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> values

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> selected points

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> MultHigh for Data Acquisition</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Labeled dataset <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, unlabeled dataset <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, query size <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, committee size <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             Train a committee of <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> models <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{1},M_{2},\dots,M_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{1},M_{2},\dots,M_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in U</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Compute confidence <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> from each model <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Compute minimum confidence across all models: <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\min}(x)=\min_{i}c_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\min}(x)=\min_{i}c_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             Select top-<math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> points with highest <math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\min}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\min}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> values

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> selected points

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
