<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Results for Active Learning</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix section, we provide detailed results across all datasets for active learning. We find similar trends across various datasets and models as seen in the main paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Experiment Setup Details</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Folktables Subset.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the “New Mexico” state subset for both ACSIncome and ACSEmployment throughout the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choosing Rashomon parameter <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To make sure the Rashomon set contains enough models for each algorithm in our setup while keeping the threshold tight, the value of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen to be the smallest value possible such that there are at least <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> models in the Rashomon set for each setup. The <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> value is chosen separately for each setting, i.e., each random seed, initial dataset size, and number of steps; but is shared between all different algorithms, i.e., a common Rashomon parameter <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is used across algorithms for any particular setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>All Results for ACSIncome Dataset</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide detailed results for active learning on the ACSIncome dataset.
First, we restate the results in Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Controlling Multiplicity During Active Learning ‣ 5 Multiplicity and Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, along with the standard deviations recorded separately, present in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.2 All Results for ACSIncome Dataset ‣ Appendix C Additional Results for Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
We then repeat the experiments in Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.3 Controlling Multiplicity During Active Learning ‣ 5 Multiplicity and Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(d, e) for LR and MLP models, and the results are presented in Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ C.2 All Results for ACSIncome Dataset ‣ Appendix C Additional Results for Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure">
