</span></p></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Accuracy and ambiguity across multiple steps of data acquisition for LR (top, (a), (b)) and MLP (bottom, (c), (d)) models for ACSIncome dataset. Similar trends persist across multiple steps of active learning.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>All Results for ACSEmployment Dataset</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide detailed results for active learning on the ACSEmployment dataset.
First, we repeat the experiments in Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Controlling Multiplicity During Active Learning ‣ 5 Multiplicity and Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, along with the standard deviations recorded separately, present in Figure <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.3 All Results for ACSEmployment Dataset ‣ Appendix C Additional Results for Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
We then repeat the experiments in Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.3 Controlling Multiplicity During Active Learning ‣ 5 Multiplicity and Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(d, e) for all three model types, and the results are presented in Figure <a href="#A3.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ C.3 All Results for ACSEmployment Dataset ‣ Appendix C Additional Results for Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
