</span></p></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Accuracy and ambiguity across multiple steps of data acquisition for RF (top, (a), (b)), LR (middle, (c), (d)) and MLP (bottom, (e), (f)) models for Bank dataset. Similar trends persist across multiple steps of active learning.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Results for Data Imputation</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix section, we provide detailed results across all datasets for data imputation. We find similar trends across various datasets and models as seen in the main paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Experiment Setup Details</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Folktables Subset.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Same details as above in §<a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Additional Results for Active Learning ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choosing Rashomon parameter <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Same details as above in §<a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional Results for Data Imputation ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>All Results for Bank Dataset</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we first repeat the experiments in Figure <a href="#S6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 6.2 Experiment Setup and Algorithms ‣ 6 Multiplicity and Data Imputation ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for the Bank dataset and provide the results in Figure <a href="#A4.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ D.2 All Results for Bank Dataset ‣ Appendix D Additional Results for Data Imputation ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
Next, we repeat the experiments in Figure <a href="#S6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 6.2 Experiment Setup and Algorithms ‣ 6 Multiplicity and Data Imputation ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> for the Bank dataset using RandomForests, and the results are presented in Figure <a href="#A4.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ D.2 All Results for Bank Dataset ‣ Appendix D Additional Results for Data Imputation ‣ Data as a Lever: A Neighbouring Datasets Perspective on Predictive Multiplicity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</p>
</div>
